.DS_Store
.env

odoo-db-dump/
data/
logs/
certs/

*.tgz
*.zip
*.gz

# moved-aside PG14 datadirs from the PG15 bump (Module 28)
clinic/data/postgresql.pg14*

# generated sink connectors carry an injected password - regenerate with scripts/generate-local-sink-connectors.sh
sync/local/connectors/generated/

# Same rule, CLOUD side (F-010). generate-sink-connectors.sh writes
# mysql-sink-<table>.json straight into cloud/connectors/ - NOT into a
# generated/ subdir - with connection.password already substituted. On the mini
# that is 19 files carrying the live sink DB password, in a tracked directory,
# in a repo whose origin is public. A single `git add -A` there publishes them.
# The *.json.template and known-good.json files do NOT match this pattern.
cloud/connectors/mysql-sink-*.json
cloud/connectors/generated/
# The hub's OTHER rendered connectors (register-odoo.sh / _render_connector.py
# write odoo-*.json with live passwords), its untracked htdocs copy, its starter
# SQL and every *.bak-* the operator leaves behind. These rules lived only on the
# retired node/cloud branch; when the hub checked out the shared branch on
# 2026-09-15 (Stage 4) 19 node-local files surfaced as untracked, five of them
# carrying credentials. Templates and known-good.json stay tracked: ignore rules
# never apply to tracked files.
cloud/connectors/odoo-*.json
cloud/htdocs/
cloud/openelis-starter.sql
*.bak-*

# Same rule again, CLINIC side. scripts/generate-connectors.sh renders
# debezium/local/connectors/mysql-source-connector.template.json into BOTH paths
# below, and its SUBST_VARS includes ${LOCAL_DEBEZIUM_PASSWORD} -- so the output
# carries the live Debezium password. These two were TRACKED in this public repo
# until 2026-09-14, surviving only because someone had hand-edited the committed
# copies to say ${DEBEZIUM_DB_PASSWORD} instead, a variable the generator does not
# substitute (and which is not set in .env at all). That left the repo in a state
# where the committed file could not register and the working file could not be
# committed: running the generator and then `git add` leaked the credential.
# Template is tracked, output is not. Regenerate rather than copy.
clinic/connectors/mysql-source-connector.json
clinic/connectors/mysql-local-source-connector.json

# The bahmni-config service's entrypoint REWRITES whatever tree is mounted at
# /usr/local/bahmni_config. docker-compose.override.yml points it here so it can
# never touch bahmni_config/ again - so this tree is churn the service owns,
# regenerated on every boot, and must never be committed.
.local-config-scratch/

# scripting jars for the Filter SMT: fetch with config/kafka-connect/ext/fetch-scripting-jars.sh
clinic/config/kafka-connect/ext/*.jar
# Some nodes keep the scripting jars one level up instead of in ext/ (Ghated
# does). Rule ported from node/ghated on 2026-09-14 when that node moved to
# this branch and three downloaded jars appeared as untracked: its own
# .gitignore had covered them and this one did not. Already-tracked files are
# unaffected by a new ignore rule, so config/kafka-connect/sync-origin-customizer.jar
# stays tracked -- that one is a BUILD ARTIFACT WE SHIP, not a download.
clinic/config/kafka-connect/*.jar
*.pyc

# --- Rendered MirrorMaker config (2026-09-14) --------------------------------
# scripts/setup-mirrormaker.sh renders these from the .template files beside
# them. They are per-node OUTPUT and must never be committed: both copies were
# tracked until today carrying a real remote broker host and this node's
# consumer group id, so a fresh clinic cloned another node's identity, and two
# clinics sharing one MirrorMaker consumer group id split the partitions
# between them and each sees only half its own changes.
#
# ORDERING: config/mirrormaker/mm2.properties is BIND-MOUNTED by
# docker-compose.yml:453. Docker creates a DIRECTORY at a bind-mount source
# that does not exist, so `setup-mirrormaker.sh` must run BEFORE the first
# `docker compose up` on a new node -- otherwise MirrorMaker starts against an
# empty directory. (That failure is what the old install-clinic.sh warning was
# describing when it called this path "an empty DIRECTORY in the tree".)
# Rendered MirrorMaker config, both paths. setup-mirrormaker.sh produces these
# from the .template files beside them; they are per-node OUTPUT carrying a real
# broker host and this node's consumer group ids, so they must never be
# committed -- a fresh clinic was inheriting another node's identity from them,
# and two clinics sharing one MirrorMaker consumer group id split the partitions
# between them and each sees half its own changes.
#
# The main path stayed tracked until the template could actually regenerate it.
# It can now (fixed in d47be8e), and that was VERIFIED ON BOTH NODES before
# untracking: 55 settings each side on Rawach and on Ghated, none missing, none
# extra, the single difference being the order of alternatives inside one topics
# regex, compared as a set and found identical.
#
# ORDERING: config/mirrormaker/mm2.properties is BIND-MOUNTED by
# docker-compose.yml:453. Docker creates a DIRECTORY at a bind-mount source that
# does not exist, so setup-mirrormaker.sh must run BEFORE the first
# `docker compose up` on a new node.
clinic/config/mirrormaker/mm2.properties
sync/local/mirrormaker-config/mm2.properties

# clinic installer: composed or hand-written answers and the seed's password file
# carry live credentials and must never reach this (public) repo.
clinic-*.env
secrets.env
# the installer's podman->docker shim (lib.sh mk_podman_shim); a per-node artifact, never config
clinic/install/.bin/
# rendered per-clinic clinlims up-sinks (install-clinic.sh join copies the tracked
# clinic/connectors/clinlims-ghated-sink-all.json with the slug swapped), like odoo-*.json above
cloud/connectors/clinlims-*.json

# hub/ (2026-09-17): the sync layer's own compose project, split out of cloud/.
# Same secret classes as the cloud/connectors/* rules above -- the env file,
# the JAAS SASL password, and every connector JSON a generator writes with a
# live password already substituted. Templates are exempt by name: the six
# hand-authored connector JSONs below carry only ${VAR} placeholders (verified
# 2026-09-17), substituted by register-odoo.sh at registration time, not at
# rest -- so they stay tracked.
hub/.env
hub/kafka_server_jaas.conf
hub/connectors/mysql-sink-*.json
hub/connectors/odoo-*-sink-all.json
hub/connectors/clinlims-*-sink-all.json
hub/connectors/mysql-cloud-source-connector.json
!hub/connectors/odoo-cloud-source.json
!hub/connectors/clinlims-cloud-source.json
!hub/connectors/odoo-cloud-sink-all.json
!hub/connectors/clinlims-cloud-sink-all.json
!hub/connectors/odoo-ghated-sink-all.json
!hub/connectors/clinlims-ghated-sink-all.json
